@page "/products"
@* POLICY gate instead of a role gate. The page names only the policy; the framework
   resolves policy → DepartmentRequirement → DepartmentHandler (all wired in Program.cs).
   Reach for a policy when the rule is more than a role name — here, "is in the Inventory
   department," read from a claim. Roles answer "who are you?"; policies answer arbitrary
   "are you allowed to?" questions. *@
@attribute [Authorize(Policy = "CanManageInventory")]

<PageTitle>Products</PageTitle>

<h1>Products</h1>

<p>Inventory management -- only accessible to users in the Inventory department.</p>

